%% DM26-0670

%% The whole bootstrap of a Polar cluster from the sandbox-local target, in three phases.
%% Steps marked (new) are the proposed Flux deployment and are not built. The rest runs today
%% (infra/up.nu, traced in docs/architecture/cluster-bootstrap.md).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Op as Operator
    participant Up as infra/up.nu
    participant Host as Host services<br/>registry :5000<br/>deployment git server (new)
    participant K as Kubernetes API
    participant Flux as Flux controllers (new)
    participant W as Polar workloads

    Op->>Up: nu infra/up.nu sandbox-local --user U --email E

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over Op,W: PHASE 1 - before Flux. up.nu does what cannot be GitOps
    Up->>Host: build and push images, start the registry<br/>(infra/images.nu, just registry-up)
    Up->>Up: render the manifests (infra/render.nu)<br/>split them into layers (infra/layers.nu) (new)
    Up->>Host: sign, commit and push the layers to the deployment repo (new)
    Up->>K: apply namespaces, make the cluster CA,<br/>create the secrets (polar-admin-grant, secrets.nu)
    Up->>K: install Flux, give it the repo's address and certificate (new)
    end

    rect rgb(215, 227, 190)
    Note over Op,W: PHASE 2 - Flux. Layers are reconciled in order
    Flux->>Host: pull the deployment repo over mTLS (new)
    Flux->>K: apply platform, cert-issuer, data, cassini, identity, agents,<br/>each after the one before is healthy (new)
    K->>W: pods start and get their certificates
    Up->>K: wait until every layer reports Ready (new)
    end

    rect rgb(204, 220, 232)
    Note over Op,W: PHASE 3 - after Flux. up.nu does what needs running workloads
    Up->>W: port-forwards, then the admin flow (accounts and certificates)
    Up->>W: sign and push the first policy to the schedules repository
    Up->>Op: ask to close the browser, import the certificate, check Neo4j
    Up->>Op: report that the target is up
    end
